    "inscription": "Original--Recto:inscribed in pencil in LC:Princess Marie Ther\u00e9se de Lamballe, (illegible) of Queen Marie Antoinette/1749 - 1792In Plate--inscribed under image on left:Peint d'apres nature a Paris en 1789 par Anton Hickel Peintre de laCour de Vienne./Mar. Ther. Louisa of Savoy Carignan,/ PRINCESS of LAMBALLE./ Born at Turin in 1749 &amp; massacred at Paris Sep,,r 3, 1792./She fell victem to her attachment to the Queen of France, whom even impending Death could/not induce her to calumniate.;inscribed under image at right: S. Malgo, Sculp. / Mar.Ther.Louise de Savoye Carigan./ PRINCESSE de LAMBALLE/ N\u00e9e \u00e0 turin en 1749 et massacree a Pari le 3.Sep,,1792./Victime de son attachement pour laReine de France, elle aima mieux mourir que/calomnier so maitresse.; inscribed in LC:Quand un Monstre \u00e0 l'honneur presit des attentats,/ On presente sa t\u00eate, et l'on n'obeit pas.-La Harpe. /London, Published as the Act directs March 22, 1793 by S. Malgo, No. 57 Titchfield Street\nMarks: Stamped in brown ink on verso:R.I.S.D./MUSEUM/OF ART surrounded by PROVIDENCE/RHODE ISLAND all inscribed in a circle",
